WEBVTT


00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:03.030
We think Einstein was probably
a good kisser.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.000
He's rumoured to have said,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.260
'Everything should be made as simple as possible,
but not simpler.'

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.860
Whether it was him
or some other genius

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.540
with a brain the size of a planet,
it's still good advice.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.220
So make short,
simple words your first choice.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.400
They're the most powerful.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.020
Just look in any dictionary.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:30.320
Short words have the longest entries.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.100
It's easy to think that
long words make you sound

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.800
smarter or more important.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.610
But why use your brain to translate

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.375
a short word into a long one?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.460
Your readers will only have
to use their brains

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.750
to translate it back again.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.800
Your good ideas will shine through

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.230
in clear,
straightforward language.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.410
No one's saying you have to use short words

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.370
all the time.
That would be boring.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.490
Remember that quote:
'Everything should be made as simple

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.640
as possible,
but NOT simpler.'

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.590
Sometimes,
you might need to use longer

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.250
words or technical jargon
words if they're

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.280
right for your reader.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.910
But when you do,
think of each jargon word

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.340
as a stepping stone
that moves the reader

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.290
towards your meaning.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.950
You want to make the spaces
in between the stepping stones as

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.560
easy to cross as possible.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.580
So, look at
the words in between and make

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.030
sure they're as short
and simple as they can be.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.960
You don't have to be Einstein
to have big ideas,

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.020
or to do a great job.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:40.770
But think of him when you're
writing at work, and then KISS.

